## NEW — coder-executability blockers (E-series) → see review § "Coder-executability findings"

Since Dean's F1/F2 adjudication, a second review lens was run: a 4-agent **coder-simulation** pass
(can a coder *build* §5–§7 at the sites the plan names?), re-verified against `main@9906dac5`. It
found **five additional MAJOR blockers**, added to the review as a distinct **§ Coder-executability
findings (E-series)** (with a Verdict pointer + a disposition bullet). Please fold these in the
**same planner pass** as F1/F2 — they are more blocking than F3–F12 (they stall or silently break a
coder on Commit 1/2), and **all fixes are plan revisions; none instructs the coder directly.**

Read the review's E-series section for the file:line detail and the exact per-finding plan edit;
headlines only here (single-source — do not re-derive from this handoff):

- **E1** — §5-1b writes `req.Anchor = copy(baseResult)` inside `runAnalyzersAndScore`, which has no
  `req` and doesn't build the request (that's `collectV2ModelRequest:607`). Needs a build-site
  change + return-signature threading (~19 call sites, 4 test files) and an explicit ban on the
  `namedResults[0]` shortcut (which silently sources anchor-(a) from TA in the TA-only path).
- **E2** — `withSatEntry` (used 87×) + PD/V2 siblings never set `Anchor`; Commit 2's reroute makes
  every fixture skip → all optimizer tests **and the #1513 goldens** go red. Fix = in-body
  `req.Anchor` set (signature unchanged, §11-compatible) + add the 4 fixture files to §6 + make §9's
  grep case-insensitive. (Distinct from the goldens Finding-2 compile note.)
- **E3** — `copy(baseResult)` is invalid Go; no `Clone` exists; shallow copy aliases the stored sat
  result → (b)-overwrite mutates it (ships silently; bites PR-2). Needs explicit deep-copy + a PR-1
  no-mutation assertion.
- **E4** — §6-2c routes `AcceleratorName`/`Cost`/`Utilization` "from `req.Anchor`," but those are
  `VariantCapacity` fields (`vc.X`; two don't compile on `AnalyzerResult`, `Utilization` is silently
  model-level) — leave `:283/:284/:302` as `vc.X`; and the removed nil-guard lets an empty-ballot
  `req.AnalyzerResults[0]` panic — needs a length guard.
- **E5** — §7's field-classification test has no observable anchor at the §5/§10 build site, and the
  TA-only fixtures need anchor≠ballot but `withSatEntry` ties them → vacuous pass. Needs an
  engine-package test off `collectV2ModelRequest` + a distinct-results fixture builder.

Minor (E6–E13) + two extensions of existing findings (F8 real headings/4-site spread; F12 adds the
`saturation-scaling-config.md:255-259` "not yet consumed" stale block) are in the same section —
polish for the same pass.

